From: Linux Fieldwork <fieldwork@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] vmspawn: skip namespace entry when no user namespace exists

For ordinary bind mounts, start_virtiofsd() can be called with both source and
target UIDs invalid. In that case no user namespace is allocated, but the child
still calls namespace_enter() with userns_fd == -EBADF. An unprivileged caller
then receives the helper's synthetic EPERM before virtiofsd can start.

Only enter a user namespace when one was actually allocated. The translated
and foreign-UID paths keep their existing namespace transition and subsequent
mount-namespace setup.

This candidate is retained against canonical systemd commit
1652be7df88d358c1e215c7de5431505348e5ab3. It is not an upstream submission.
---
 src/vmspawn/vmspawn.c | 22 ++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vmspawn/vmspawn.c b/src/vmspawn/vmspawn.c
--- a/src/vmspawn/vmspawn.c
+++ b/src/vmspawn/vmspawn.c
@@ -1,17 +1,19 @@
         if (r < 0)
                 return r;
         if (r == 0) {
                 /* Child */
 
-                r = namespace_enter(
-                                /* pidns_fd= */ -EBADF,
-                                /* mntns_fd= */ -EBADF,
-                                /* netns_fd= */ -EBADF,
-                                userns_fd,
-                                /* root_fd= */ -EBADF);
-                if (r < 0) {
-                        log_error_errno(r, "Failed to enter user namespace for virtiofsd: %m");
-                        _exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
+                if (userns_fd >= 0) {
+                        r = namespace_enter(
+                                        /* pidns_fd= */ -EBADF,
+                                        /* mntns_fd= */ -EBADF,
+                                        /* netns_fd= */ -EBADF,
+                                        userns_fd,
+                                        /* root_fd= */ -EBADF);
+                        if (r < 0) {
+                                log_error_errno(r, "Failed to enter user namespace for virtiofsd: %m");
+                                _exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
+                        }
                 }
 
                 if (userns_fd >= 0 && unshare(CLONE_NEWNS) < 0) {
-- 
2.51.0
